\b WHAT HAPPENS\b0\par
\tab Only notes that are listed and ticked are changed. Notes hidden by a filter are never changed.\par
\tab Resolving adds a "resolved" comment to the note, under your name, as Paratext does. Your comment, if you typed one, comes just before it.\par
\tab Assigning adds a comment that assigns the note. Without a comment of yours it says "Assigned to ...". Choose (nobody) to remove the assignment.\par
\tab A note you resolve or assign is marked as read for you, its new comment included: you must have read it to decide. Notes that needed no change keep their read status.\par
\tab Notes that need no change (already resolved, or already assigned to that person) are left as they are and listed in Results.\par
\tab After the change the tool reads the notes again and lists any note Paratext did not change, so you can check it.\par
\tab If you are an observer of the project, the notes are listed but the buttons are off.\par
\tab With several projects, each project is changed on its own: if one cannot be changed (for example because you are an observer there), the others still are.\par
\tab Nothing is lost: every change is a new comment, so the note's history stays complete. A resolved note can be opened again in Paratext.\par
The notes go through Paratext itself, so they are shared by Send/Receive like any other change to notes.\par
